---
import TumLogo from "./TumLogo.astro";
import coverage from "../../data/coverage-summary.json";

const rows = [...coverage.per_exam].sort((a, b) => b.pct - a.pct);
---

<footer class="sources">
  <div class="sources-inner">
    <TumLogo />
    <div class="sources-cols">
      <div>
        <h4>Sources</h4>
        <p class="src-line">
          Twelve past IN2228 papers (2020–2025) plus all eight SS26 exercise sheets with their
          official solutions. Codes read <b>year · kind · examiner</b>:
          <span class="src">25EDC</span> = 2025 <b>E</b>ndterm, examiner <b>DC</b> (Prof. Daniel
          Cremers) · <span class="src">23RLI</span> = 2023 <b>R</b>etake, <b>LI</b> (Dr. Haoang Li)
          · <span class="src">20MFB</span> = 2020 <b>M</b>idterm, <b>FB</b> (Florian Bernard) ·
          <span class="src">EX05</span> = exercise sheet 5.
        </p>
        <div class="coverage">
          <h4>Coverage</h4>
          <p>
            <b>{coverage.overall_pct}%</b> of past-exam sub-questions are cited directly ({
              coverage.cited
            }/{coverage.detected}), and <b>89–98%</b> of every Cremers paper; the rest are folded
            into merged cards or covered by the recaps. The 2022 endterm is a scan with no text
            layer — it is covered, but cannot be measured automatically.
          </p>
          <div class="cov-chips">
            {rows.map((r) => <span class="cov-chip">{r.exam} {r.pct}%</span>)}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>About</h4>
        <p>
          Revision deck for <b>3D Computer Vision (IN2228)</b>, TU&nbsp;München. Answers follow the
          <b>official sample solutions</b>; for variant phrasings the scoring points are merged.
          Items tagged <span class="src-ai">AI-generated</span> are model-written practice and are
          not from past exams.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every examiner writes a different paper, so each question carries the examiner's initials
          and the ones by the <b>current examiner</b> are marked ★ and sorted first.
        </p>
        <p>
          Formulas rendered with <a href="https://katex.org/" rel="noopener">KaTeX</a> at build
          time. Built from the official course materials for personal study.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="sources-bar">
    TUM IN2228 · 3DCV Exam Q&amp;A · for educational use only — not affiliated with or endorsed by
    TUM.
  </div>
</footer>
